Problem Statement
Simulate passenger movement (boarding and alighting) across a sequence of bus stops, maintain continuous passenger count, enforce vehicle seating capacity constraints, and flag any instances of capacity overload.

2. Objectives
•	Track real-time passenger occupancy across bus routes.
•	Detect capacity overloads dynamically at each stop.
•	Summarize peak occupancy and total passengers served.

3. Assumptions
•	Passenger count cannot drop below zero.
•	Bus capacity is fixed at 40 seats.

4. Algorithm
1. Initialize current passengers = 0, MAX_CAPACITY = 40.
2. Read route data list of tuples: (Stop Name, Boarding, Alighting).
3. At each stop: current = current - Alighting + Boarding.
4. If current < 0, adjust current = 0 (error recovery).
5. If current > MAX_CAPACITY, flag overload condition.
6. Track peak passenger count across entire trip.
